/Title (To study the career pathways in low-code development, to identify the skills required for different roles, and to understand the future growth and evolution of low-code platforms.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 444 0 R
>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<<
/Title (Low-code development is an approach to building software applications mainly through visual tools and configuration instead of writing large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled using visual development environments, predefined components and templates. Typical building blocks include forms for capturing data, reports and dashboards for viewing it, and workflows that define how information moves through a business process.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 445 0 R
/Next 546 0 R
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Title (However, low-code does not remove the need for technical understanding. Concepts such as data models, logic, integration and security remain important, and developers who understand programming and technical principles are better able to design applications, extend them where the platform falls short and resolve problems when they occur.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 445 0 R
/Prev 546 0 R
>>
endobj
